-## Configuration
-
-Simulation inputs live in `config.toml`. Countries, operators, simulation duration, scale factors, architecture choices, and mobility settings are configured there.
-
-```toml
-[countries.spain]
-enabled = true
-data_dir = "data/spain"
-mcc = 214
-
-  [countries.spain.operators]
-  movistar = { id = 7, enabled = true }
+julia --project=. -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.instantiate()'
+julia --project=. scripts/download_data.jl    # CORA v1.0 release, SHA-256 checked
+julia --project=. main.jl                     # menu
+julia --project=. main.jl national spain      # or call a run directly
 ```
 
-Data follows this layout:
-
-| Path | Purpose |
-| --- | --- |
-| `data/<country>/opencellid/<mcc>.csv` | OpenCellID attachment-point records used as location proxies |
-| `data/<country>/municipalities.csv` | standardized municipality population and coordinates |
-| `data/<country>/regions.geojson` | municipality or county boundaries |
-| `data/processing_scripts/` | Python preprocessing tools for raw geographic datasets |
+Countries, operators, duration, scale and mobility settings live in `config.toml`.
+Input data goes under `data/<country>/` (OpenCellID CSV, `municipalities.csv`,
+`regions.geojson`); the preprocessing scripts are in `data/processing_scripts/`.
 
